From: Balázs Gyimesi <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: qualcomm: rmnet: size the deaggregated copies for buffer reuse

An offload engine on the device's receive handler (Qualcomm NSS) keeps a
packet's buffer as one of its own receive buffers if it is at least its
receive buffer size, and frees a smaller one, allocating a new empty buffer
in its place. Allocate the copies at that size (a module parameter,
0 keeps the exact size).
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/rmnet/rmnet_map_data.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/rmnet/rmnet_map_data.c
@@ -17,6 +17,17 @@
 #define RMNET_MAP_DEAGGR_SPACING  64
 #define RMNET_MAP_DEAGGR_HEADROOM (RMNET_MAP_DEAGGR_SPACING / 2)
 
+/* An offload engine on the device's receive handler (Qualcomm NSS) keeps a
+ * packet's buffer as one of its own receive buffers instead of handing it
+ * back, if the buffer is at least its receive buffer size (1792 bytes plus
+ * NET_SKB_PAD); a smaller one is returned and freed, and a new empty buffer
+ * is allocated for the engine in its place. Size the copies for that; 0
+ * keeps the exact size.
+ */
+static unsigned int rmnet_deagg_min_alloc = 1856;
+module_param_named(deagg_min_alloc, rmnet_deagg_min_alloc, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(deagg_min_alloc, "minimum allocation of a deaggregated packet (0: exact)");
+
 static __sum16 *rmnet_map_get_csum_field(unsigned char protocol,
 					 const void *txporthdr)
 {
@@ -390,7 +401,8 @@
 	if (!packet_len)
 		return NULL;
 
-	skbn = alloc_skb(packet_len + RMNET_MAP_DEAGGR_SPACING, GFP_ATOMIC);
+	skbn = alloc_skb(max_t(u32, packet_len + RMNET_MAP_DEAGGR_SPACING,
+			       rmnet_deagg_min_alloc), GFP_ATOMIC);
 	if (!skbn)
 		return NULL;
 
